          %p
            Accordingly, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+parallel+transport"} higher parallel transport
            induced by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat c(\nabla)
            over 3-dimensional manifolds
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo :
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : \Sigma \to X
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            called
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+field"} gauge field
            called the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} supergravity C-field
            in certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            theories. In particular, if (with due care) one takes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∇
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
            to be the
            %em
              universal connection on the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+principal+bundle"} universal principal bundle
            over a smooth version of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat c(\nabla)
            is the background
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+field"} gauge field
            for bare
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
          %p
            Therefore this structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat c(\nabla)
            has become known as the
            %strong Chern-Simons 2-gerbe
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∇
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
            %em
              Chern-Simons
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} circle 3-bundle
            \.
          %p
            At least for simply connected
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            one may enhance the assignment
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo ↦
                  %mover
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla \mapsto \hat c(\nabla)
            to a morphism of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mi conn
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mi diff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 3
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\hat \mathbf{c} : \mathbf{H}_conn(X,\mathbf{B}G)
                  \\to \mathbf{H}_{diff}(X,\mathbf{B}^3 U(1))
                  \\,,
          %p
            where on the left we have the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            of smooth
            = succeed "-principal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
