          %h2#constructions Constructions
          %h3#in_differential_geometry__for_lie_groups In differential geometry – For Lie groups
          %h4#InCechDelineCohomology In Cech-Deligne cohomology
          %p
            In (
            %a{:href => "#GeomConstructionFirst"}> Brylinski-McLaughlin I
            ) there is spelled out an explicit construction of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat c(\nabla)
            for given
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∇
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
            in
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne+cohomology"} Deligne cohomology
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#CechCocyclesForCharClasses"} Brylinski-McLaughlin II
          %p
            In this section here we review this explicit cocycle construction. In the
            %a{:href => "#InInfChernWeil"} next section
            we discuss a systematic way to derive this construction.
          %p
            Assume that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply+connected"} simply connected
            compact simple
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+group"} spin group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            to be that whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transgression"} transgression
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            has as image in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+cohomology"} de Rham cohomology
            the de Rham class of the normalized canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} Lie algebra cocycle
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu \in CE(\mathfrak{g})
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to X
            a
            = succeed "-bundle" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∇
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}
            such that we have a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech cohomology
            cocycle for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            given by a smooth transition function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %mi j
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo ∩
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi j
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  g_{i,j} : U_i \cap U_j \to G
          %p
            satisfying on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo ∩
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi j
                  %mo ∩
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i \cap U_j \cap U_k
            the cocycle condition
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mi k
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_{i j} \cdot g_{j k} = g_{i k}
          %p
            Since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is assumed connected and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply+connected"} simply connected
            and since for every Lie group the second
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group"} homotopy group
            is trivial we have that the first nonvanishing homotopy group of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is the third one.
          %p Therefore we can always find (possibly after refining the cover) a lift of this cocycle as follows:
          %ul
