          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech cohomology
              cocycle with coefficients in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mn 3
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^3 \mathbb{R}/\mathbb{Z}
              which is given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                        %mi k
                        %mi l
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mn 3
                    %msubsup
                      %mover
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                        %mi k
                        %mi l
                      %mo *
                    %mi μ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi mod
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    c(g)_{i j k l} := \int_{\Delta^3} \hat g_{i j k l}^* \mu
                    \\;\;\;\;\; mod \mathbb{Z}
            %p
              is well defined and represents the class
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 4
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c(P) \in H^4(X)
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+cohomology"} integral cohomology
            %p
              Moreover, this refines to the cocycle in Cech-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne+cohomology"} Deligne cohomology
              that is given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi CS
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi σ
                        %mi i
                        %mo *
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mo ∫
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mn 1
                      %mi CS
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi P
                      %mo ⋅
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo *
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mo ∫
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mn 2
                      %mi CS
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi P
                      %mo ⋅
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                          %mi k
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo *
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mo ∫
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mn 3
                      %msubsup
                        %mover
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                          %mi k
                          %mi l
                        %mo *
                      %mi μ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi mod
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left(
                    CS(\sigma_i^* A)
                    \\,,\;\;
                    \\int_{\Delta^1} CS((P\cdot \hat g_{i j})^* A)
                    \\,,\;\;
                    \\int_{\Delta^2} CS((P\cdot \hat g_{i j k})^* A)
                    \\,,\;\;
                    \\int_{\Delta^3} \hat g_{i j k l}^* \mu
                    \\;\;\; mod \mathbb{Z}
                    \\right)
                    \\,,
            %p where
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi P
                        %mo ,
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \Omega^1(P,\mathfrak{g})
                  is the incarnation of the connection
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∇
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
                  as an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ehresmann+connection"} Ehresmann connection
                  given by a glbally defined 1-form on the total space
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to X
                  of the bundle;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi σ
                          %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo →
                        %mi P
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_i : U_i \to P
                  are the local
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to X
                  that induce the original Cech cocycle
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi g
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mi j
                          %mo :
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi σ
                            %mi i
                          %mo ⋅
                          %msubsup
                            %mi σ
                            %mi j
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (g_{i j} := \sigma_i \cdot \sigma_j^{-1})
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                        %mo ⋅
                        %msub
                          %mover
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                        %mo :
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mn 1
                        %mo →
                        %mi P
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \cdot \hat g_{i j} : \Delta^1 \to P
                  is given by the right
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
                  and analogously for the other terms;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi CS
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo .
                        %mo .
                        %mo .
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CS(...)
                  denotes the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+form"} Chern-Simons form
                  of the given
                  = succeed "-valued" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝔤
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              First notice that this is indeed well-defined: by compactness and simplicty of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              we have
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 3
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_3(G) = \mathbb{Z}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi μ
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mn 3
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu \in \Omega^3(G)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 3
                      %mo →
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : S^3 \to G
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∫
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 3
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mi μ
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int_{S^3} f^*\mu \in \mathbb{Z} \subset \mathbb{R}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c(g)
              is indeed a Cech cocycle.
            %p
              Then the proof is effectively just the observation that the given collection of differential forms indeed does refine this to a Cech-cocycle with coefficients in the Deligne complex, and that therefore we can read off the image of the integral cohomology class
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [c(g)]
              in de Rham cohomology from the curvature 4-form of this Deligne cocycle. That is by construction
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mo ∇
                      %mo ∧
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mo ∇
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %mo ∈
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi cl
                        %mn 4
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle F_\nabla \wedge F_\nabla \rangle \in \Omega^4_{cl}(X)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Weil+theory"} Chern-Weil theory
              is indeed the image of the claimed integral class.
          %p
            So the only mystery about this construction is really: where does it come from? Apart from making this clever Ansatz and checking that it works, can one somehow systematically derive this construction? This we shall try to answer the section
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#InInfChernWeil"} below
          %h4#InInfChernWeil
            In
            = succeed "-Chern-Weil" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            The above Cech-Deligne cocycle construction of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat c(\nabla)
            may be understood as a special case of the general construction of Chern-Weil homomorphisms by the methods discussed at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Weil+theory"} ∞-Chern-Weil theory
          %p We briefly recall the general approach and then spell out the details.
          %p
